      "reason_summary": "Both historians agree the target '爰' (in Liu Xiaobiao's annotation quoting 陶侃別傳: '庾翼薨表其子爰') is an abbreviated personal name referring to 庾爰之 (園客), son of 庾翼. Historian A's record is more precise: the surface form of the referent is '爰之' (the full personal name being abbreviated), and the antecedent_hint is '爰之' which correctly identifies the antecedent within the annotation text. Historian B's surface_form '庾爰之' adds the surname 庾 which is not present in the surface form of the referent as it appears; the canonical_hint '庾爰之' already carries the full name. Historian B also adds a redundant third relation (same_person to '爰之') which duplicates the identity already established by the canonical_hint and the kinship relation. Historian A's two relations (kinship to 庾翼, same_person to 園客) are sufficient and well-supported by the evidence. The discourse.antecedent_hint '爰之' in Historian A is more appropriate since the antecedent in the annotation context is the name 爰之 appearing in the 氏譜 annotation, not 庾翼. Historian A's record is the more accurate and economical representation.",
